{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And the sense of <b>beyond what his hand attains</b>: an obligation to give according to his wealth and also according to the days of the vow, whether many or few. And the section of the Priestly Blessing was juxtaposed to the section of the nazirite because once the Torah of the nazirite, who is holy, was completed, the Torah of the priests, who are holy, was mentioned. And the disputants said that this blessing was [one] the priest would pronounce over every meal-offering bringer, and it was juxtaposed because of 'according to what the hand of the vow-maker attains.' But the truth is as our Sages of blessed memory transmitted, and the proof is 'Aaron lifted his hands toward the people and blessed them' (Leviticus 9:22) on the eighth day, and this section was written [in the context of] the commandment at the erection of the Tabernacle, that Aaron bless the people. And there it says נשיאות כפים, for כפים are like ידים; only ידים is the general term."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The phrase מלבד אשר תשיג ידו (Numbers 6:21) is rendered from the lemma as written; the verse means the nazirite brings offerings 'beyond what his hand attains,' i.e., according to his means."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:43.830629663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}